  "note": "寻风地带 (native:lancheng/huanying … calm_east; 第十章 A): up the mirror's polished yellow-stone way (幻影道: incense, a mist lying on the ground, the walls shining) onto a high field under low cloud; wind-worn pillars of warm white stone standing like people, grooved on the windward face, moss on the lee; waist-high grass combed one way, mist in long streaks running with the wind between the pillars (all of it reads the map's guiding wind: WorldMapWinds); three sheltered hollows north, still and flowered; the 逆灵宫's black altar at the downwind west edge, black banners, charm ash and the rings they drew; the 兵部's dead camp on the east, its tents in strips, a broken flag, a cold stove of stones, a frozen scout. Old and used: trodden trails, bleached stumps, a cairn someone built on the way up.",
